id: pm-slack-3e7d
title: Keep enabled Slack lifecycle notifications durable across restarts
description: "Persist Slack-only delivery intents, idempotency identities and acknowledgments. Existing immediate retry/backoff remains transport logic; pm-observer owns evidence-note delivery into PM only. CLI lifecycle hooks currently send without a durable receipt; sibling pm-slack-standup builds digests rather than delivering lifecycle intents. No duplicate open outbox item found; tracker-reconciliation items are excluded."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:00:45.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T22:05:17.621Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Crash/retry fixtures produce one acknowledged send; ambiguous remote outcomes remain visible; notification failure never rolls back a committed item.; Typed SDK and agent-sized CLI output, typed refusals with remedies, README and example, no-git regressions, public tracker copy validation, unchanged npm and Bun CI release gates."
comments[32]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:01:09.181Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: CLI lifecycle hooks expose successful command results but no Slack-specific durable delivery acknowledgment. pm-slack currently retries immediate HTTP attempts only. pm-observer src/delivery.ts and src/store.ts own idempotent PM evidence notes, and pm-slack-standup owns digests. This feature owns Slack delivery intents and receipts only. Plan: opt-in durable storage, atomic claims and idempotency, persisted uncertain outcomes with explicit reconciliation, bounded SDK and CLI inspection/drain, real no-git tracker regressions and public tracker-copy validation. Reconciliation PR items remain untouched."
  "2026-10-21T20:09:32.697Z",codex-agent,"Implemented SQLite FULL-synchronous durable delivery with atomic cross-process claims and frozen history-revision identities, explicit enable boundary, verified SDK history recovery for commits missed by hooks, bounded structured inspection, safe destination fingerprints, and explicit reconciliation of uncertain sends. Targeted lifecycle/corpus/transport tests: 215 passed, 0 failed; index.ts and outbox.ts each measured 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Typecheck and docstring gate passed. Full unchanged release gates will run under npm and Bun in CI because local CPU is saturated."
  "2026-10-21T20:16:31.480Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation used a read-only non-git archive of the public pm-slack tracker at f4dce1dcf2b291a99d6c9e3f99fb529b104c707f: 85 items, 515 history entries, 177 immutable source files. Scan inspected all 515 entries and queued zero pre-enable events. Real-data snapshot intents produced 85 acknowledged localhost sends, zero duplicate sends after reopening and re-draining, with all source bytes unchanged. Bounded inspection returned 10 rows and omitted 75. Native Bun acceptance also recovered one lifecycle event with one acknowledged send and zero duplicates without git. Receipt pagination now makes every retained key reachable."
  "2026-10-21T20:16:33.696Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: independently removing enqueue persistence, forgetting durable acknowledgment, removing verified history recovery, or bypassing durable hook integration makes the corresponding outbox regression fail. Source functions were restored after each proof. No dependency pin was changed; the declared compatibility floor is aligned to the pinned 2026.10.15 SDK used for verified history recovery. Local strict health has pre-existing global-extension version skew and installer fence drift; CI checks a clean clone after installation. Linked tests passed 9 of 9; test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so results are recorded here without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-21T20:25:41.778Z",codex-agent,"Installed CLI validation in a plain scratch tracker confirmed compact TOON (217 bytes for empty status), JSON (255 bytes), operation without a git executable, and typed disabled refusals exiting 2 with an explicit enable remedy. The pinned host generic renderer omitted null fields and appended generic output after direct printing; a renderer scoped only to slack outbox now owns TOON. The pinned host generic thrown-error path reduced extension errors to command_failed, so this command returns typed structured nonzero refusal receipts. These host UX gaps were worked around without changing the CLI repository. Native Bun uses its own synchronous SQLite API; Node uses node:sqlite. No standalone lint script exists: local lint evidence is the docstring gate plus git diff --check."
  "2026-10-21T20:26:28.966Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted production-source coverage: 216 passed, zero failed, skipped or canceled; index.ts and outbox.ts each measured 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Current typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint passed (76 documented declarations). All five behavioral reverts fail independently, including restoring the Node-only SQLite loader under native Bun; every function and emitted artifact was restored. Native Bun acceptance passes with git absent. CLI refusals now preserve producer codes and remedies in structured nonzero results. Full npm and Bun release gates remain delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:56.376Z",codex-agent,"Implementation committed as 0403120189a39ffb76d495324b24ffe4b7334a90 and proposed in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/147. Initial CI is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/39670707658 and runs unchanged npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 plus native Bun acceptance. Awaiting full-gate completion; tracker reconciliation items remain byte-for-byte untouched."
  "2026-10-21T20:32:32.416Z",codex-agent,"Full implementation CI passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/39670707658 at 0403120189a39ffb76d495324b24ffe4b7334a90. Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 283 tests per gate, zero failed/skipped/canceled, and 100 percent lines/branches/functions. Native Bun acceptance passed in both jobs. Documentation in docs/outbox-validation.md records measured public-data validation and five revert proofs. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/147 will retain final-head CI evidence. Automated review remains missing: Greptile trial expired, Sourcery budget-limited, CodeRabbit skipped, cubic neutral. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains open, with no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T22:08:33.230Z",codex-agent,"PR #147 follow-up: copy pm-starter .hound.yml verbatim to disable jshint on deliberately committed ES2022 dist output. Branch already contains origin/main. Latest CodeRabbit body (comment 6325847600) reports automatic review skipped because the repository has fewer than 10 stars; no review findings or inline CodeRabbit comments exist. No behavioral fix or revert regression is required for this configuration-only change. Targeted checks run locally; CI remains the full npm/Bun release gate. The package currently has typecheck and docstring checks but no standalone ESLint script."
  "2026-10-21T22:09:17.080Z",codex-agent,"Added .hound.yml byte-for-byte from pm-starter, retaining its rationale comment and jshint.enabled=false. Local validation: reference byte comparison passed; npm run docstring passed (8 files, 76 declarations); git diff --check passed; node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-slack-3e7d --run --progress passed both linked commands: node --test test/outbox.test.ts (10 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled) and npm run typecheck. Initial linked run refused the inherited command because this fresh checkout has a detached ref; after inspecting and acknowledging the existing commands in this clone, rerun passed. Existing policy disables stored test-run receipts, so results are recorded here. No function changed; behavioral revert proof is not applicable. CI will run the unchanged full npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains nonterminal."
  "2026-10-21T22:16:00.488Z",codex-agent,"CodeRabbit completed full review 5606899987 on 801fcf8 and posted one valid finding (discussion_r4342530828): sendOutbox validates every route before sending, so an invalid unrelated route raises invalid_input before a request, but drain currently marks the row ambiguous. Plan: reset every typed OutboxError pre-request refusal to pending, clear owner, undo attempts and rethrow; retain ambiguity for ordinary transport errors. Add a real non-git tracker and localhost HTTP regression for malformed unrelated routing, prove it fails with only drain reverted, then rerun targeted checks and final-head CI. Earlier Hound-only head passed full npm/Bun CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/39684455606 (283 tests per gate on Node 22 and 26)."
  "2026-10-21T22:17:52.248Z",codex-agent,"Fixed the valid CodeRabbit pre-request refusal finding: every typed OutboxError resets the claimed row to pending with owner cleared and attempts decremented before rethrow; ordinary transport exceptions remain ambiguous. Documented the send callback contract and rebuilt committed dist output. New real non-git tracker/localhost integration regression checks two invalid unrelated-route drains send zero requests and preserve the pending receipt at zero attempts, then routing repair acknowledges exactly one request without manual reconciliation or duplicates. Behavioral revert proof: reverting only drain's condition to the original destination_changed-only handling makes the new regression fail (missing invalid_input refusal); restored code passes. node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-slack-3e7d --run --progress passed all 3 linked commands: outbox suite 11/11, typecheck, and isolated regression 1/1. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run docstring (76 declarations), native Bun acceptance (1 recovered, 1 acknowledged, 0 duplicates, no git), and git diff --check passed. Full unchanged npm/Bun gates remain delegated to final-head CI. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays nonterminal."
  "2026-10-22T09:39:18.674Z",pi-agent,"Review round on PR 147: three unresolved CodeRabbit threads remain after the pre-request refusal fix. Latest CodeRabbit review body has no outside-diff findings. Plan: verify each thread against the current drain and transport code, fix the valid ones with regressions that fail on behavioural revert, then rerun the unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-22T09:53:27.878Z",pi-agent,"Verified the three unresolved CodeRabbit threads against the current head. No outside-diff findings were in the latest CodeRabbit review body.\n\nPRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vA2RC is valid: the published SDK example caught OutboxError and exited 0. The example now sets process.exitCode from the refusal. The same example also treated a pre-request fetch failure as an uncertain throw; it now returns retry for ENOTFOUND, EAI_AGAIN and ECONNREFUSED by socket code.\n\nPRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vA2RG is valid: postToSlackOnce dropped the socket error code, and sendOutbox marked every non-HTTP failure ambiguous. Classification now uses the preserved cause code. A 503 body containing ENOTFOUND stays ambiguous. Timeouts, resets and other response errors stay ambiguous.\n\nPRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vA2RJ is valid: a retry continued posting later rows in the same drain. drain now stops after a retry. A blanket stop would leave every later destination behind a persistently refused oldest row, so the next drain orders by attempts, then rowid. One refused destination cannot block every other notification on the following drain.\n\nBehavioural revert proof, each function restored after the failure:\n- classifyOutboxSendError pre-request branch reverted: transport regression failed, actual ambiguous, expected retry.\n- postToSlackOnce cause removed: transport regression failed, actual cause code undefined, expected ECONNREFUSED.\n- drain break removed: retry regression failed, actual sends first and second, expected first only.\n- drain order reverted to rowid: retry regression failed, next drain sent first, expected second.\n- example exitCode removed: example regression failed, actual exit 0, expected 2.\n- example fetch classification removed: example regression failed, pending count actual 0, expected 1."
  "2026-10-22T10:04:14.269Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: remote head pulled and main is already contained. Read every comment on all three unresolved threads and the latest CodeRabbit review (no outside-diff findings). Retaining the reviewed draft fixes; independently verifying regressions, behavioral reverts and unchanged full npm/Bun gates. Earlier draft evidence remains append-only."
  "2026-10-22T10:05:43.454Z",codex-agent,"Independent continuation verification: all 15 outbox tests pass. Six individual behavioral reverts each fail their targeted regression: retry classification, preserved transport cause, stop after retry, fair next-drain ordering, example refusal exit status, and example pre-request classification. Each source was restored in a finally block. Whole-PR self-review found a related gap: a response reset after headers had no response error listener. Added a real partial-response/reset regression and reject that error conservatively as ambiguous so the drain can finish and continue later rows."
  "2026-10-22T10:08:21.725Z",codex-agent,"Partial-response behavioral revert proof: removing only postToSlackOnce response error handling leaves the actual HTTP reset pending indefinitely; node --test --test-force-exit --test-timeout=15000 --test-name-pattern=\"pre-request transport codes\" test/outbox.test.ts exits 1 with one canceled timeout. Restored code completes the same regression successfully (1 passed). This timeout is the deliberately reverted defect, not a host-load gate failure. Seven individual reverts have now demonstrated the regressions. All mutations restored."
  "2026-10-22T10:13:30.717Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged npm release gate passed under isolated HOME with git global/system config disabled: 288 tests passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled; index.ts and outbox.ts each 100% lines/branches/functions; 77 documented declarations, audit 0 vulnerabilities, pack 14 files, changelog and both release workflow checks passed. Pinned pm test --run --progress passed all 7 linked commands, including 15/15 outbox tests and native Bun acceptance (1 recovered event, 1 acknowledged send, zero duplicates, no git). Linked result persistence remains disabled by existing policy; the CLI reports tracking_disabled. Full Bun release gate is running. Local pm health found ignored/global pm-github host-version skew plus installer fence drift; verifying clean-checkout health with isolated HOME to exclude local extension state."
  "2026-10-22T10:14:09.429Z",codex-agent,"Clean-checkout tracker health passed: pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers returned exit 0 with all 10 checks ok after installing the pinned merge mappings under isolated HOME. Remaining telemetry-queue, stale-work and historical provenance notices are advisory; history and integrity passed. No history rewrites, extension changes or telemetry configuration changes were made."
  "2026-10-22T10:16:47.787Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round gates passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 288 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled, 100% lines/branches/functions for both production modules at unchanged thresholds. Both commands ran with isolated HOME and disabled git global/system configuration. npm ci, all 7 linked commands, native Bun acceptance, clean-clone strict health (10 checks ok), generated dist, and diff checks passed. No host-load gate retries were needed. Seven independent behavioral revert proofs are recorded above; no deliberately reverted source remains. All three thread findings are fixed, latest review has no outside-diff findings, and whole-PR review added the partial-response fix. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Releasing the claim; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T19:18:37.756Z",codex-agent,"Additional orchestrator round: worktree is clean at bdba3b4, no unpushed commits, remote pulled and main already contained. Previous fixes and evidence remain intact. Read every comment on both new unresolved threads; latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings. PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vJoJ9 is valid: receipt existence uses an unindexed tuple predicate per recovered transition. PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vJoKG is valid: DNS may fail with EAI_AGAIN as well as ENOTFOUND. Plan: shared immutable key derivation and indexed existence lookup, actual SQLite query-plan regression, and a deterministic temporary-DNS-failure fixture that exercises the relaxed assertion and retry classification."
  "2026-10-22T19:21:16.693Z",codex-agent,"Both new fixes verified. receiptKey preserves the existing SHA-256 tuple encoding and is shared by enqueue and has; existence now uses the delivery primary key. Real non-git tracker regression inserts 64 receipts, locks the existing key format, checks present/absent revisions and read-only behavior, and runs EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN on the actual SQL observed during has (all database operations remain real). Before the fix and when reverting only has: actual SCAN delivery, expected indexed SEARCH, regression exits 1. Restored code passes. DNS assertion now accepts ENOTFOUND or EAI_AGAIN and verifies retry classification. A custom lookup on a real HTTP Agent deterministically returns EAI_AGAIN; reinstating only the old ENOTFOUND assertion makes that regression exit 1 with EAI_AGAIN versus ENOTFOUND. Restored code passes both regressions (2/2); combined transport/lookup regressions pass 3/3. Every revert restored in finally. Whole-PR self-review checked every receipt query and DNS assertion: no other per-transition unindexed lookup or strict unresolvable-host assertion remains; exact status counts intentionally aggregate retained rows, while receipt reconciliation/enqueue use keys and pagination uses rowid. No dependency pins or thresholds changed; installed pinned dependencies verified."
  "2026-10-22T19:26:38.054Z",codex-agent,"Additional-round final gates passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 290 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled; index.ts and outbox.ts remain 100% lines/branches/functions at unchanged thresholds. Both run under isolated HOME with git global/system config disabled. All 8 pm-linked commands passed, including 17/17 outbox tests, both new regressions 2/2, typecheck and native Bun acceptance (1 recovered, 1 acknowledged send, 0 duplicates, no git). Clean-clone pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes all 10 checks, with existing stale-work/provenance advisories only. Build, 77-declaration docstring gate, audit (0 vulnerabilities), package (14 files), changelog and release workflow checks passed. No gate retries were needed. Both behavioral reverts fail independently as documented above and every source was restored; generated dist rebuilt. Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings; all current unresolved findings are addressed. Existing policy disables persisted linked-run receipts, so results are recorded here. Previous round work is preserved. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress."
  "2026-10-22T20:26:13.821Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator follow-up: clean worktree at 045fb25, remote pulled; merging current main before implementation. All five supplied findings will be verified and addressed within the durable outbox scope, with independent behavioral revert proofs. GitHub GraphQL currently refuses review-thread reads because the shared account API rate limit is exhausted; supplied orchestrator findings and local code are available, so implementation proceeds without treating missing review access as approval."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:21.181Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all five supplied findings. Destination changes now park refused receipts at zero added attempts and continue; explicit skip records skipped without claiming delivery, and restoring the original route permits explicit retry. Ambiguous outcomes hold later rows for the same destination within a drain, while reads never drain and lifecycle hooks attempt at most one request. Reconciliation has an explicit force override for verified PID reuse through SDK and --force-reconcile; the default still protects active senders. Recovery stages each verified history file before publication, isolates bad streams, drains healthy queued/new receipts, and exposes recovered.failed with a nonzero history_unavailable partial report in JSON and TOON. Recovery eligibility is snapshotted at enable; explicit configure records a future-only epoch, so widening filters before the first scan cannot backfill stale messages. Existing SDK queues without saved policy still drain; enable/configure adopts future history. Policy lookup is indexed per timestamp so concurrent future configuration is observed without receipt-table scans. SDK example handles partial recovery and parked refusals with nonzero exit status. Core suite passed 234 tests with 100% lines/branches/functions for index.ts and outbox.ts; new directed suite passed 11 tests and SDK incomplete-history example passed separately. GitHub API access recovered: all review threads/comments were fetched with complete pagination; no unresolved GitHub threads remain. Latest CodeRabbit body is empty and latest substantive body has no outside-diff findings; neither substitutes for review of this new patch."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:28.069Z",codex-agent,"Eleven independent behavioral revert proofs completed; every mutation was restored in finally before builds. (1) Restore pending/rethrow for destination_changed: channel/webhook regressions fail, drain exits 2 instead of 0 and healthy rows are starved. (2) Remove per-destination ambiguity hold: outage callback runs twice instead of once. (3) Restore draining reads: get sends 1 instead of 0. (4) Remove hook limit: lifecycle hook sends 20 instead of 1. (5) Remove force override from resolve: reused-PID SDK reconciliation throws in_flight. (6) Disconnect CLI force flag: explicit CLI reconciliation exits 2 instead of 0. (7) Abort on the first bad history file: only 1 instead of 2 healthy receipts acknowledges. (8) Abort CLI draining on global history failure: only 1 instead of 2 queued receipts sends across the regression. (9) Apply current filters to retained history: widening before first recovery sends 4 stale/eligible events instead of the single historically eligible event. (10) Remove SDK example refused exit status: exit 0 instead of 2. (11) Remove SDK example partial-history handling: healthy verified receipt sends 0 instead of 1. Regression commands are node --test --test-name-pattern with the corresponding descriptive names in test/outbox.test.ts. No history records were rewritten. Main merge completed without conflicts or pending merge receipts; local host extension/fence skew is isolated for clean-clone health verification."
  "2026-10-22T21:04:21.698Z",codex-agent,"Final follow-up validation passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 302 tests passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled; both index.ts and outbox.ts retain 100% lines/branches/functions at unchanged thresholds. Both release gates completed on the first final run under isolated HOME and disabled git global/system config. All 9 linked commands pass across the initial run and focused retry: outbox suite 29/29, focused supplied-finding regressions 14/14, prior indexed/DNS regressions 2/2, native Bun acceptance 1 recovered event/1 acknowledged send/0 duplicates/no git, and remaining focused checks/typecheck. The full linked outbox command timed out twice at 120 seconds during parallel host load; retrying only that command with a per-run 300-second window passed in 83.282 seconds, with no source, metadata or assertion changes. Clean-clone pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passed all 10 checks, only the existing historical provenance advisory remains. Docstrings cover 81 declarations; production audit reports 0 vulnerabilities; package contains 14 files; committed dist rebuilt. Eleven independently failing behavioral revert proofs above are restored. No additional unresolved GitHub threads or outside-diff findings were present at the complete review read. Existing tracking_disabled policy prevents linked-run receipt persistence; explicit results are retained here. All five supplied findings and related SDK example paths are fixed. No dependency, telemetry, provenance history or threshold changes; no thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Releasing the claim; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T21:46:38.842Z",codex-agent,"New CodeRabbit follow-up: pulled ca217bc with clean worktree and no unpushed commits; origin/main is already contained. Reusing this item and preserving completed rounds. Plan: forbid SDK example fetch redirects with a real redirect regression; date initial reviewer availability separately from later review rounds; separate retained-history failures from SQLite receipt storage errors, with real database fault regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Both full release gates will run at unchanged thresholds after the fixes."
  "2026-10-22T21:50:27.063Z",codex-agent,"Verified all comments on the three current unresolved threads and latest substantive CodeRabbit body; no outside-diff findings. PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vYUNt: published example fetch now uses redirect:error; a real 307 POST to a closed-port target is retained ambiguous, never marked pending or resent automatically. PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vYUN_: reviewer availability is explicitly the initial 2026-10-21 run, as introduced by d1f60cc; later completed CodeRabbit reviews on 2026-10-22 and their findings are distinguished. PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vYUOD: all receipt database accesses during capture use a narrow storage boundary, preserving typed OutboxErrors and converting database exceptions to storage_unavailable with a local runtime storage remedy. Retained-history read/verification failures keep their separate isolation behavior. Focused regressions pass 5/5 using real non-git SDK trackers, a localhost redirect, and real SQLite missing-table, busy-write and read-only-write faults. Removing each fault permits recovery from byte-identical history. Typecheck, test compilation, diff check and the 82-declaration docstring gate pass. Whole-PR self-review found no other fetch redirect or storage/history error-boundary instance in scope."
  "2026-10-22T21:50:31.061Z",codex-agent,"Four independent behavioral revert proofs fail with exit 1: removing only redirect:error makes the published-example regression report ambiguous=0 instead of 1; restoring only captureSlackOutbox from ca217bc makes all three real SQLite fault subtests fail with Missing expected rejection because the faults become failed history counts; removing only the outbox.has storage guard fails the missing-receipt-table case; removing only the enqueue storage guard fails both busy-write and read-only-write cases. Every temporary mutation was restored in finally before any build or gate. Exact regression commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"holds redirects as ambiguous\" test/outbox.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"actual SQLite receipt faults\" test/outbox.test.ts. The documentation correction is checked against its 2026-10-21 introduction and the later dated 2026-10-22 completed review, rather than a test that merely repeats prose."
  "2026-10-22T21:56:45.585Z",codex-agent,"Initial full npm and Bun release gates both passed 307 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations and 100% production lines/branches/functions; all 10 linked commands passed, including 34 outbox tests and 5 new regression tests, with no timeout. Self-review then hardened the redirect fixture against ephemeral port reuse by keeping its refused target reserved until the source listener binds. Assertions and production code are unchanged. Rechecking all four behavioral reverts and the focused tests, then rerunning both full release gates against this final deterministic fixture. Existing linked-result persistence remains tracking_disabled; results are recorded here."
  "2026-10-22T22:05:13.589Z",codex-agent,"Final gates after the deterministic redirect fixture adjustment: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 307 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled, with 100% lines/branches/functions for index.ts and outbox.ts at unchanged thresholds. All 10 linked commands passed, including 34 outbox tests, 14 prior focused regressions, 5 new regressions, typecheck and native Bun acceptance (1 recovered lifecycle, 1 acknowledgment, 0 duplicates, no git). The latest five-test linked command passed again after fixture adjustment; all four behavioral revert proofs were rechecked and restored before the final gates. No test timeouts or failure retries were needed this round; the two full gates were repeated solely after hardening fixture port allocation. Clean-clone pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes all 10 checks, with the existing historical provenance advisory only. Docstring gate: 82 declarations; production audit: 0 vulnerabilities; package: 14 files; generated dist rebuilt. Current reviewer-availability correction is grounded in the dated initial document and later completed CodeRabbit review. All three requested threads are addressed; latest review has no outside-diff findings. Existing tracking_disabled policy prevents persisted linked-run receipts, so exact results and commands are recorded here. No new out-of-scope issue was found. Releasing the claim without closing the item; it remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. No thread replies/resolutions, merge, release, dependency bump, telemetry change or history rewrite."
